s, but ultimately failed and lost Naples in 1424. He recaptured it in 1442 and was crowned king of Naples. He had good relations with his vassal, Stjepan Kosača, and his ally, Skanderbeg, providing assistance in their struggles in the Balkans. He led diplomatic contacts with the Ethiopian Empire and was a prominent political figure of the early Renaissance, being a supporter of literature as well as commissioning several constructions for the Castel Nuovo.","wp_description":"King of Aragon from 1416 to 1458","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_V_of_Aragon","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/Scuola_napoletana_forse_da_piero_della_francesca%2C_ritratto_di_alfonso_d%27aragona%2C_1450-60_ca._%28parigi%2C_mus%C3%A9e_jacquemart-andr%C3%A9%29_03.JPG","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Scuola_napoletana_forse_da_piero_della_francesca%2C_ritratto_di_alfonso_d%27aragona%2C_1450-60_ca._%28parigi%2C_mus%C3%A9e_jacquemart-andr%C3%A9%29_03.JPG/960px-Scuola_napoletana_forse_da_piero_della_francesca%2C_ritratto_di_alfonso_d%27aragona%2C_1450-60_ca._%28parigi%2C_mus%C3%A9e_jacquemart-andr%C3%A9%29_03.JPG","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1416,"display_to":1458}